==Swedish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sv|svenne banan}}
* {{l|sv|svennebanan}}

===Etymology===
Used by immigrants in [[w:Sweden|Sweden]] in reference to ethnic Swedes. It originates from a [[nickname]] for ''[[Sven]]''.<sup>[citation needed]</sup>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|[ˈsvɛ̀nːɛ]}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{lb|sv|derogatory|humor|slang}} an ethnic/native [[Swede]] (as opposed to immigrants to Sweden)

====Usage notes====
The word has acquired or developed two different meanings, which sometimes merge. One meaning refers to [[w:ethnicity|ethnicity]], merely indicating that the individual referred to is an [[w:ethnic Swede|ethnic Swede]], and the second meaning indicating that the individual referred to is boring, shy and habitually reserved. Because the latter sense is actually a common viewpoint in Sweden, both meanings combined or merged are sometimes used by ethnic Swedes, often ironically.

